          "candidate": {
            "category": "bug",
            "confidence": 84,
            "evidence": "`LOAD_FAST_LOAD_FAST` and the two borrow opcodes are indexed with `dis.opmap[...]` based only on `sys.version_info`; actual membership in `dis.opmap` is never checked. The subsequent transform filtering expects missing opcodes to have been represented as `None`, but execution never reaches it when lookup raises.",
            "file_path": "hypothesis/src/hypothesis/internal/lambda_sources.py",
            "finding": "The dynamic opcode lookup can still raise `KeyError` on an interpreter whose Python version meets the gate but whose `dis.opmap` lacks the CPython-specific opcode. This contradicts the stated fallback to `None` and can make importing this module fail, particularly on alternate Python implementations or if a later version removes an opcode.",
            "line": 106,
            "severity": "medium",
            "source_refs": [
              "hypothesis/src/hypothesis/internal/lambda_sources.py:102-143"
            ],
            "suggested_fix": "Use `dis.opmap.get(\"LOAD_FAST_LOAD_FAST\")`, `dis.opmap.get(\"LOAD_FAST_BORROW\")`, and `dis.opmap.get(\"LOAD_FAST_BORROW_LOAD_FAST_BORROW\")` directly, then retain the existing filtering of transforms containing `None`."
          },
          "finding_index": 0,
          "publish_decision": "publish",
          "suppression_reason": null
        }
      ],
